# Next open task per project · HAND-WRITTEN. Verified by rot rule R8.
#
# This file is NOT generated and never was. Do not add a comment claiming it
# is maintained by something -- the original said "maintained by `mindforge
# wrap`", wrap had never written it, and a line pointing at a closed issue sat
# at the top of every brief for 16 days because everyone assumed it was
# someone else's job. See mindforge#13.
#
# The queue cannot be generated: no tool can infer what you decided to do next.
# So it stays hand-written and becomes CHECKABLE instead -- column 5 carries a
# reference, and R8 holds it against the real tracker every session until it is
# answered.
#
# FORMAT -- five TAB-separated columns:
#   project      directory name under $MINDFORGE_PROJECTS (default ~/Programs)
#   next         the one next task, in your own words
#   impact       1-5
#   dependency   no | blocks:<what> | waits:<what>
#   ref          #<n>  checked against that project's GitHub tracker
#                -     deliberate opt-out (milestone work, no single issue)
#                BLANK IS NOT AN OPT-OUT -- R8 reports a row that forgot it.
#
# The repo is read from each project's own git remote, so the directory name
# and the repository name are allowed to differ.
#
# @priority ranks projects; earlier = stronger, and it dominates impact.
@priority project-a project-b
project-a	#12 the thing you are actually doing next	5	no	#12
project-b	v2.0.0 milestone with no single issue	3	waits:project-a#12	-
